    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d777-a3">

                <pb facs="0854" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg742"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mexican Minister in Nicaragua to Admiral
                    Kimball.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Mexico</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-12-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 30,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Rear Admiral</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge to you the receipt of the note which you were pleased to place in my
                    hands on the 24th instant, a little after 3 o’clock in the afternoon, and
                    occasioned by the visit which I had the pleasure of making to you on board the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Albany</hi> to repay a like attention which you
                    showed me on the previous day at the city of Corinto.</p>
                <p>In said note you refer to the conversation which we had, incidentally, concerning
                    the possible journey of Gen. Jose Santos Zelaya, ex-President of Nicaragua, on
                    board the Mexican man-of-war <hi rendition="#italic">General Guerrero</hi>—a
                    matter which you treated in writing, as you personally told me, for the sole
                    object of explaining your neutral attitude in the face of my purpose to give
                    asylum to said Señor Zelaya on board the <hi rendition="#italic">General
                        Guerrero</hi>, and to order said vessel to sail for Salina Cruz.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to say to you that I have taken note of the contents
                    of your communication, and I have transcribed it to my Government for its
                    information.</p>
                <p>Wherefore, I take pleasure in assuring you of my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bartolome Carbajal y
                        Rosas.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
